From dbetebenner at nciea.org  Thu Sep  8 21:27:32 2011
From: dbetebenner at nciea.org (Damian Betebenner)
Date: Thu, 8 Sep 2011 14:27:32 -0500
Subject: [datatable-help] Over-writing factors
Message-ID: <8AD9137B75B37049AA711A4B64CEDB694BF2FE5C70@AUSP01VMBX05.collaborationhost.net>

Not sure whether the following is an intended behavior with data.table. Perhaps it is something idiosyncratic with factors.
It is different than what one gets with data.frame

test.df <- data.frame(X=letters[1:10], Y=rnorm(10))
test.dt <- data.table(X=letters[1:10], Y=rnorm(10))

test.df$X <- "Something Different"
test.dt$X <- "Something Different"
Error in `[<-.data.table`(x, j = name, value = value) :
  Some or all RHS not present in factor column levels


test.df <- data.frame(X=letters[1:10], Y=rnorm(10))
test.dt <- data.table(X=letters[1:10], Y=rnorm(10))

test.df[["X"]] <- "Something Different"
test.dt[["X"]] <- "Something Different"




